1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,360
Quentin Tarantino, one of the most acclaimed filmmakers of all time, known for bringing

2
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:09,040
his bold ideas to life with surreal visuals and mind-bending storytelling.

3
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:11,160
But he wasn't always a Hollywood icon.

4
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:14,520
Once he was just an ordinary guy working at a video store.

5
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:17,040
Until one night he decided to rewrite his story.

6
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:22,200
And there was like one night, stay up all night long and rather than give myself excuses,

7
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:27,100
I would look at everything that I'm up in my life or everything I'm not doing or whatever

8
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:29,940
and just not give myself any excuses out.

9
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:30,940
Just like nail it.

10
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:35,939
And I would spend like all night laying out everything I'm doing that's wrong.

11
00:00:35,939 --> 00:00:38,860
And then I would spend the last two hours figuring out how I can change it.

12
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:43,580
And as opposed to just doing it and then going to get some sleep, I decided to change my

13
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:44,580
life.

14
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:46,580
Today I present you the Tarantino Method.

15
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:48,740
To follow this process you'll need three things.

16
00:00:48,740 --> 00:00:51,419
A pen, a notepad, and the dead of night.

17
00:00:51,419 --> 00:00:54,220
When the world is silent and now the soul is awake.

18
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:55,500
That's when it can happen.

19
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:56,500
Trust.

20
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:57,500
The journey begins.

21
00:00:57,500 --> 00:00:59,299
The first page is always going to be the hardest.

22
00:00:59,299 --> 00:01:03,220
But it's really all about getting that ball rolling.

23
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:08,699
Now that you've started, you have to ask yourself the big, scary, fear-mongering question.

24
00:01:08,699 --> 00:01:10,660
What am I doing wrong?

25
00:01:10,660 --> 00:01:11,940
Be brutally honest.

26
00:01:11,940 --> 00:01:14,940
As Quentin himself would say, nail it.

27
00:01:14,940 --> 00:01:15,940
Take your time.

28
00:01:15,940 --> 00:01:16,940
Dive deep.

29
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:17,940
It's gritty.

30
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:18,940
It's tough.

31
00:01:18,940 --> 00:01:20,940
But it's absolutely necessary.

32
00:01:20,940 --> 00:01:27,099
And when you push through, boom, you're halfway there.

33
00:01:27,099 --> 00:01:28,220
It's all out there.

34
00:01:28,220 --> 00:01:29,220
The fears.

35
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:30,220
The doubts.

36
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:31,220
The mistakes.

37
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:32,220
The lessons.

38
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:33,220
The heartbreak.

39
00:01:33,220 --> 00:01:34,220
All laid out.

40
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:35,220
Bare for you to see.

41
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:36,220
Not built up in your mind.

42
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:38,220
But on paper.

43
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:39,580
Tangible.

44
00:01:39,580 --> 00:01:40,580
Take a moment.

45
00:01:40,580 --> 00:01:42,540
Because now you have to ask yourself.

46
00:01:42,540 --> 00:01:44,699
How can I change it?

47
00:01:44,699 --> 00:01:46,680
We're not all Quentin Tarantino.

48
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:49,019
You might be feeling like you're all written out.

49
00:01:49,019 --> 00:01:50,699
So let's make this part simple.

50
00:01:50,699 --> 00:01:52,300
A straightforward list.

51
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:54,500
A hundred ways you can change your life.

52
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:56,339
Quite a simple process.

53
00:01:56,339 --> 00:01:59,860
Take a mistake you've learned, and write down a way to change it.

54
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:00,860
Repeat it.

55
00:02:00,860 --> 00:02:02,540
Over and over again.

56
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:03,540
Push forward.

57
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:04,540
Write it down.

58
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:05,540
Adapt.

59
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:06,540
Reflect.

60
00:02:06,540 --> 00:02:07,540
Learn.

61
00:02:07,540 --> 00:02:08,539
And grow.

62
00:02:08,539 --> 00:02:11,139
Until finally, when you ask yourself, how can I change my life, you'll have a hundred

63
00:02:11,139 --> 00:02:12,139
ways to do it.

64
00:02:12,139 --> 00:02:15,740
But there's one very important thing you need to remember throughout this whole night.

65
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:18,740
You gotta actually f***ing do it.

66
00:02:20,699 --> 00:02:23,740
You gotta f***ing do it.


